{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And bricks, they say to us.</b> The taskmasters <b>say</b>, as at the first count." "<b>And your people's sin.</b> If it had a patach, I would say it is construct state — 'and this thing is the sin of your people.' Now that it has a kamatz, it is a noun, and this is its meaning: 'and this thing brings sin upon your people,' as if written וְחַטָּאת לְעַמֶּךָ; like ״כְּבֹאָנָה בֵּית לֶחֶם״ (Ruth 1), which is like לְבֵית לֶחֶם — and so many."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:40.538243281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}